{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And a man went.</b> Rabbi Yehuda bar Bizna said: what is 'went'? That he went following his daughter's counsel. It was taught: Amram was the greatest of the generation. When he saw Pharaoh's decree, he divorced his wife. They all arose and divorced their wives. Miriam said to him: Father, your decree is harsher than Pharaoh's, for Pharaoh decreed only against the males, but you decree against the males and against the females. Pharaoh decreed only in this world, but you decree in this world and in the world to come. Amram went and took back his wife, and they all took back their wives. And according to the plain sense, this event was before Pharaoh's decree, for Aaron and Miriam were born to them earlier; rather, when it came to tell what happened to them at the time of the decree concerning their sons, it began to tell also from the beginning of their marriage."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:12.744089282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}